# Expose the Culprit, mode 2 alone: "Exile any number of face-up creatures you control with disguise in a face-down pile, shuffle
# that pile, then cloak them" (CR 701.58a, 701.58b). Bot1 has two Riftburst Hellions: the first was cast face down (Black Lotus)
# and turned face up on turn 5 for its disguise cost, the second was cast face down on turn 7. On turn 9 Bot1 casts a Concealed
# Weapon face up (it has disguise but is not a creature) and the Expose the Culprit. Only a face-up creature with disguise may be
# chosen: the face-down Hellion (a nameless 2/2, no abilities) and the Weapon are refused, the face-up Hellion is chosen and comes
# back as a cloaked face-down 2/2, so no face-up Hellion is left and both are face down.

